{"description": "The proposed strategy is refuted even for n=2: marks at 1/5, 2/5 give pieces 1/5,1/5,3/5, and Xiang's single cut halving 3/5 yields pieces 3/10,3/10,1/5,1/5, which pair up, so Liu gets only 1/2 < 3/5.", "quote": "The strategy is to mark points at 1/(2n+1), 2/(2n+1), ..., n/(2n+1)."},
{"description": "No argument whatsoever is given for either bound; both are explicitly deferred, and the claimed small-case verifications are unsubstantiated numerical assertions.", "quote": "Need to prove both that Liu Bang can guarantee at least this much (lower bound) and that Xiang Yu can prevent Liu Bang from getting more (upper bound)."}
